IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division D: sections 33, 34, 36 and 37. LAYER 1, from the text alone.
--
-- Section 33 says how and when a self-employed person pays the contributions: the whole amount by the balance-due day
-- (a small amount, or a person who owes no income tax instalments), two thirds by December 31 (farmers and fishers), or
-- four quarterly instalments (everyone else), with the remainder by the balance-due day. Section 34 charges interest on
-- what is paid late and limits the instalments on which interest runs. Section 36 applies Income Tax Act provisions to the
-- contributions as though they were tax, and section 37 says which debt a payment goes to.
--
-- Whether a person "is required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments", or is a person "to whom
-- section 155 applies" (a farmer or fisher), are facts of an Act that is not deposited: plain inputs. The prescribed rate of
-- interest is Regulations section 36 (piece cr1): a plain input. A rate is a fraction per annum (5% is 0.05).
-- Interest is simple, over a 365-day year, counted in days (fork F2, the same reading as subsection 21(6)).
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a date is a DATE; a count of due dates n is 1 to 4, and any other n is not covered (NOTHING).

§ `Division D -- paying the contributions`

§§ `s 33 -- how and when to pay`

-- src:795 | Payment of contributions
-- src:796 | 33 (1) If the amount of the contributions required to be made by a person for a year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings is $40 or less, or a person who is required by this Act to make contributions for a year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings is not required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments for that year in respect of the person’s income tax, the person shall, on or before the person’s balance-due day for the year, pay to the Receiver General the whole amount of the contributions.
-- src:797 | Farmers and fishers
-- src:798 | (2) Every person to whom section 155 of the Income Tax Act applies, other than a person to whom subsection (1) applies, shall pay to the Receiver General on or before December 31 in each year, two thirds of
-- src:799 | (a) the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person; or
-- src:800 | (b) the contributions required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year.
@ref Act s 33(1), (2) (src:795-800)
DECLARE `cp2 Way of paying self-employed contributions` IS ONE OF
    `pay the whole amount on or before the balance-due day (subsection 33(1))`
    `pay two thirds on or before December 31 in each year (subsection 33(2), farmers and fishers)`
    `pay four quarterly instalments in the year (subsection 33(3))`

-- (1) applies to a small amount ($40 or less) or to a person not required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay
-- income tax instalments for the year; (2) to a person to whom section 155 applies, other than a person to whom (1) applies;
-- (3) to every other person.
@ref Act s 33(1), (2), (3) (src:795-811)
GIVEN `the amount of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments for the year in respect of income tax` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not deposited
      `section 155 of the Income Tax Act applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not deposited
GIVETH A `cp2 Way of paying self-employed contributions`
`s 33 — how the person must pay the contributions` `the amount of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the person is required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments for the year in respect of income tax` `section 155 of the Income Tax Act applies to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` AT MOST 40 THEN `pay the whole amount on or before the balance-due day (subsection 33(1))`
        IF (NOT `the person is required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments for the year in respect of income tax`) THEN `pay the whole amount on or before the balance-due day (subsection 33(1))`
        IF `section 155 of the Income Tax Act applies to the person` THEN `pay two thirds on or before December 31 in each year (subsection 33(2), farmers and fishers)`
        OTHERWISE `pay four quarterly instalments in the year (subsection 33(3))`

-- src:795 | Payment of contributions
-- src:796 | 33 (1) If the amount of the contributions required to be made by a person for a year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings is $40 or less, or a person who is required by this Act to make contributions for a year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings is not required by section 155 or 156 of the Income Tax Act to pay instalments for that year in respect of the person’s income tax, the person shall, on or before the person’s balance-due day for the year, pay to the Receiver General the whole amount of the contributions.
@ref Act s 33(1) (src:795-796)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day the person died, if the person has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33(1) — the last day for paying the whole amount of the contributions` year `the day the person died, if the person has died` MEANS
    `s 2(1) — the balance-due day of a person for a year` year `the day the person died, if the person has died`

-- (2): "two thirds of (a) the contributions required ... as estimated by the person; or (b) the contributions required ... for the
-- preceding year". The "or" is read as the person's choice of base (fork F20).
-- src:797 | Farmers and fishers
-- src:798 | (2) Every person to whom section 155 of the Income Tax Act applies, other than a person to whom subsection (1) applies, shall pay to the Receiver General on or before December 31 in each year, two thirds of
-- src:799 | (a) the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person; or
-- src:800 | (b) the contributions required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year.
@ref Act s 33(2) (src:797-800)
DECLARE `cp2 Base of the two-thirds payment` IS ONE OF
    `two thirds of the contributions for the year as estimated by the person`
    `two thirds of the contributions for the preceding year`

@ref Act s 33(2) (src:797-800)
GIVEN base IS A `cp2 Base of the two-thirds payment`
      `the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 33(2) — the amount to pay on or before December 31` base `the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` MEANS
    CONSIDER base
    WHEN `two thirds of the contributions for the year as estimated by the person` THEN (`the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` TIMES 2) DIVIDED BY 3
    WHEN `two thirds of the contributions for the preceding year` THEN (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` TIMES 2) DIVIDED BY 3

@ref Act s 33(2) (src:797-800)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33(2) — the last day for the payment` year MEANS
    YearMonthDay year 12 31

-- (3): three bases. (a)(i) one quarter of the estimate on each of four days; (a)(ii) one quarter of the preceding year's amount on
-- each; (b) one quarter of the second preceding year's amount on March 15 and June 15, and on September 15 and December 15 half
-- of the amount, if any, by which the preceding year's amount exceeds half the second preceding year's.
-- src:801 | Other persons
-- src:802 | (3) Every person, other than a person to whom subsection (1) or (2) applies, shall pay to the Receiver General in respect of each year
-- src:803 | (a) on or before March 15, June 15, September 15 and December 15 in the year, an amount equal to one quarter of
-- src:804 | (i) the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person, or
-- src:805 | (ii) the contributions required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year; or
-- src:806 | (b) on or before
-- src:807 | (i) March 15 and June 15 in the year, an amount equal to one quarter of the contributions required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the second preceding year, and
-- src:808 | (ii) September 15 and December 15 in the year, an amount equal to one half of the amount, if any, by which
-- src:809 | (A) the contributions required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year
-- src:810 | exceeds
-- src:811 | (B) one half of the contributions required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the second preceding year.
@ref Act s 33(3) (src:801-811)
DECLARE `cp2 Base of the quarterly instalments` IS ONE OF
    `one quarter of the contributions for the year as estimated by the person on each of the four days`
    `one quarter of the contributions for the preceding year on each of the four days`
    `the amounts of paragraph 33(3)(b), from the second preceding year`

@ref Act s 33(3) (src:801-811)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 33(3) — the date the nth instalment is due in the year` n year MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF n EQUALS 1 THEN JUST (YearMonthDay year 3 15)
        IF n EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (YearMonthDay year 6 15)
        IF n EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (YearMonthDay year 9 15)
        IF n EQUALS 4 THEN JUST (YearMonthDay year 12 15)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref Act s 33(3) (src:801-811)
GIVEN base IS A `cp2 Base of the quarterly instalments`
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 33(3) — the instalment due on the nth date` base n `the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF n LESS THAN 1 OR n GREATER THAN 4 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER base
            WHEN `one quarter of the contributions for the year as estimated by the person on each of the four days` THEN JUST (`the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` DIVIDED BY 4)
            WHEN `one quarter of the contributions for the preceding year on each of the four days` THEN JUST (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` DIVIDED BY 4)
            WHEN `the amounts of paragraph 33(3)(b), from the second preceding year` THEN
                IF n AT MOST 2
                THEN JUST (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` DIVIDED BY 4)
                ELSE JUST ((max 0 (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` MINUS (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` DIVIDED BY 2))) DIVIDED BY 2)

@ref Act s 33(3) (src:801-811)
GIVEN base IS A `cp2 Base of the quarterly instalments`
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 33(3) — the total of the instalments due by the nth date` base n `the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF n LESS THAN 1 OR n GREATER THAN 4 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER base
            WHEN `one quarter of the contributions for the year as estimated by the person on each of the four days` THEN JUST (n TIMES (`the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated by the person` DIVIDED BY 4))
            WHEN `one quarter of the contributions for the preceding year on each of the four days` THEN JUST (n TIMES (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` DIVIDED BY 4))
            WHEN `the amounts of paragraph 33(3)(b), from the second preceding year` THEN
                JUST (((min n 2) TIMES (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` DIVIDED BY 4))
                      PLUS ((max 0 (n MINUS 2)) TIMES ((max 0 (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` MINUS (`the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` DIVIDED BY 2))) DIVIDED BY 2)))

-- src:812 | Payment of remainder of estimated contributions
-- src:813 | (4) A person referred to in subsection (2) or (3) shall also pay to the Receiver General, on or before the person’s balance-due day for the year, the remainder of the contributions as estimated under section 31. However, paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) and (3)(a) and (b) do not require the payment of any amount in respect of the person that would otherwise become due after the person’s death.
@ref Act s 33(4) (src:812-813)
GIVEN `the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated under section 31` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the parts or instalments the person was required to pay under subsection 33(2) or (3) for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 33(4) — the remainder of the estimated contributions to pay on or before the balance-due day` `the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated under section 31` `the total of the parts or instalments the person was required to pay under subsection 33(2) or (3) for the year` MEANS
    max 0 (`the contributions required for the year in respect of self-employed earnings, as estimated under section 31` MINUS `the total of the parts or instalments the person was required to pay under subsection 33(2) or (3) for the year`)

-- "paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) and (3)(a) and (b) do not require the payment of any amount in respect of the person that would
-- otherwise become due after the person's death": a part falling due on the day of death or before is still required.
@ref Act s 33(4) (src:812-813)
GIVEN `the day the part or instalment falls due` IS A DATE
      `the day the person died, if the person has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(4) — the part or instalment falling due on the day is still required` `the day the part or instalment falls due` `the day the person died, if the person has died` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the person died, if the person has died`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST died THEN `the day the part or instalment falls due` AT MOST died

§§ `s 34 -- interest`

-- (1): on the difference between the amount required and the amount paid on or before the balance-due day, from the balance-due day
-- to the day of payment, at the prescribed rate per annum (Regulations section 36, piece cr1).
-- src:814 | Interest on unpaid contributions
-- src:815 | 34 (1) If the amount paid by a person on or before the person’s balance-due day for a year on account of contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings is less than the amount of the contributions required to be made by the person, interest at a prescribed rate per annum is payable by the person on the difference between those amounts from the balance-due day for the year to the day of payment.
@ref Act s 34(1) (src:814-815)
GIVEN `the amount of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid on or before the balance-due day on account of those contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `the balance-due day for the year` IS A DATE
      `the day the difference is paid` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed rate of interest per annum` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: Regulations section 36 (piece cr1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 34(1) — the interest on the contributions unpaid at the balance-due day` `the amount of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the amount paid on or before the balance-due day on account of those contributions` `the balance-due day for the year` `the day the difference is paid` `the prescribed rate of interest per annum` MEANS
    IF `the amount paid on or before the balance-due day on account of those contributions` LESS THAN `the amount of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings`
    THEN (`the amount of the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` MINUS `the amount paid on or before the balance-due day on account of those contributions`)
         TIMES `the prescribed rate of interest per annum`
         TIMES ((max 0 (Day `the day the difference is paid` MINUS Day `the balance-due day for the year`)) DIVIDED BY 365)
    ELSE 0

-- (2): interest on a part or instalment not paid as required, "from the day on or before which the person was required to make the
-- payment to the day of payment or the beginning of the period in respect of which the person is liable to pay interest on the amount
-- under subsection (1), whichever is the earlier": the period under (1) begins on the balance-due day.
-- src:816 | Interest on instalments
-- src:817 | (2) In addition to any interest payable under subsection (1), if a person, being required by section 33 to pay a part or instalment of the contributions required to be made by the person, has failed to pay all or any part of the contributions as required, the person shall, on payment of the amount that the person failed to pay, pay interest on the amount at a prescribed rate per annum from the day on or before which the person was required to make the payment to the day of payment or the beginning of the period in respect of which the person is liable to pay interest on the amount under subsection (1), whichever is the earlier.
@ref Act s 34(2) (src:816-817)
GIVEN `the amount of the part or instalment the person failed to pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on or before which the person was required to make the payment` IS A DATE
      `the day the amount is paid` IS A DATE
      `the balance-due day for the year` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed rate of interest per annum` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: Regulations section 36 (piece cr1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 34(2) — the interest on a part or instalment not paid as required` `the amount of the part or instalment the person failed to pay` `the day on or before which the person was required to make the payment` `the day the amount is paid` `the balance-due day for the year` `the prescribed rate of interest per annum` MEANS
    `the amount of the part or instalment the person failed to pay`
        TIMES `the prescribed rate of interest per annum`
        TIMES ((max 0 ((min (Day `the day the amount is paid`) (Day `the balance-due day for the year`)) MINUS Day `the day on or before which the person was required to make the payment`)) DIVIDED BY 365)

-- (3): farmers and fishers are deemed liable to have paid by December 31 the least of (a) the contributions for the year minus $40,
-- (b) the contributions for the preceding year, and (c) the instalment stated in the Minister's notice, if there is one.
-- src:818 | Limitation for farmers and fishers
-- src:819 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), if a person is required by subsection 33(2) to pay a part or instalment of the contributions required to be made by the person in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, the person is deemed to have been liable to pay on or before the day referred to in subsection 33(2) a part or instalment that is equal to one of the following amounts, whichever gives rise to the least amount required to be paid by the person on or before that day:
-- src:820 | (a) the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, minus $40;
-- src:821 | (b) the contributions required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year;
-- src:822 | (c) the amount stated to be the amount of the instalment payable by the person for the year in the notice, if any, sent to the person by the Minister.
@ref Act s 34(3) (src:818-822)
GIVEN `the person is required by subsection 33(2) to pay a part or instalment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the instalment stated in the notice the Minister sent to the person for the year, if the Minister sent one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 34(3) — the part or instalment the farmer or fisher is deemed to have been liable to pay by December 31` `the person is required by subsection 33(2) to pay a part or instalment` `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` `the instalment stated in the notice the Minister sent to the person for the year, if the Minister sent one` MEANS
    IF `the person is required by subsection 33(2) to pay a part or instalment`
    THEN CONSIDER `the instalment stated in the notice the Minister sent to the person for the year, if the Minister sent one`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (min (`the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` MINUS 40) `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year`)
         WHEN JUST stated THEN JUST (min (min (`the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` MINUS 40) `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year`) stated)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): others are deemed liable to have paid by each of the four days the part that gives the least total by that day, out of (a) the
-- contributions for the year minus $40, (b) the contributions for the preceding year, (c) the amounts under paragraph 33(3)(b), and
-- (d) the amounts stated in the Minister's notices. Paragraphs (a) and (b) are annual amounts; the text does not say how they fall
-- across the four days, so each is divided into four equal quarters, as paragraph 33(3)(a) divides an annual amount (fork F21).
-- src:823 | Limitation for other persons
-- src:824 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2), if a person is required by subsection 33(3) to pay a part or instalment of the contributions required to be made by the person in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, the person is deemed to have been liable to pay on or before each day referred to in subsection 33(3) a part or instalment that is equal to one of the following amounts, whichever gives rise to the least total amount of those parts or instalments required to be paid by the person by that day:
-- src:825 | (a) the contributions required to be made by the person for the year in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, minus $40;
-- src:826 | (b) the contributions required in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings for the preceding year;
-- src:827 | (c) the amounts determined under paragraph 33(3)(b) in respect of the person for the year;
-- src:828 | (d) the amounts stated to be the amounts of instalment payable by the person for the year in the notices, if any, sent to the person by the Minister.
@ref Act s 34(4) (src:823-828)
GIVEN `the person is required by subsection 33(3) to pay a part or instalment` IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts stated in the notices the Minister sent to the person for the year, one for each of the four days, if the Minister sent any` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 34(4) — the total the person is deemed liable to have paid by the nth date` `the person is required by subsection 33(3) to pay a part or instalment` n `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` `the amounts stated in the notices the Minister sent to the person for the year, one for each of the four days, if the Minister sent any` MEANS
    IF `the person is required by subsection 33(3) to pay a part or instalment`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 33(3) — the total of the instalments due by the nth date` `the amounts of paragraph 33(3)(b), from the second preceding year` n `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST fromParagraphB THEN
             CONSIDER `the amounts stated in the notices the Minister sent to the person for the year, one for each of the four days, if the Minister sent any`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (min (min ((n TIMES (`the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` MINUS 40)) DIVIDED BY 4) ((n TIMES `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year`) DIVIDED BY 4)) fromParagraphB)
             WHEN JUST stated THEN JUST (min (min (min ((n TIMES (`the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` MINUS 40)) DIVIDED BY 4) ((n TIMES `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year`) DIVIDED BY 4)) fromParagraphB) (sum (take n stated)))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The part deemed due on the nth day is the difference between the totals deemed due by that day and by the day before.
@ref Act s 34(4) (src:823-828)
GIVEN `the person is required by subsection 33(3) to pay a part or instalment` IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts stated in the notices the Minister sent to the person for the year, one for each of the four days, if the Minister sent any` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 34(4) — the part the person is deemed liable to have paid on the nth date` `the person is required by subsection 33(3) to pay a part or instalment` n `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` `the amounts stated in the notices the Minister sent to the person for the year, one for each of the four days, if the Minister sent any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 34(4) — the total the person is deemed liable to have paid by the nth date` `the person is required by subsection 33(3) to pay a part or instalment` n `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` `the amounts stated in the notices the Minister sent to the person for the year, one for each of the four days, if the Minister sent any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST total THEN
        IF n EQUALS 1
        THEN JUST total
        ELSE CONSIDER `s 34(4) — the total the person is deemed liable to have paid by the nth date` `the person is required by subsection 33(3) to pay a part or instalment` (n MINUS 1) `the contributions required to be made for the year in respect of self-employed earnings` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the preceding year` `the contributions required in respect of self-employed earnings for the second preceding year` `the amounts stated in the notices the Minister sent to the person for the year, one for each of the four days, if the Minister sent any`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST earlier THEN JUST (total MINUS earlier)

§§ `s 36 and 37 -- Income Tax Act provisions, and which debt a payment goes to`

-- src:833 | Application of Income Tax Act provisions
-- src:834 | 36 Subject to this Part and except as otherwise provided by regulation, the provisions of Divisions I and J of Part I of the Income Tax Act with respect to payment of tax, assessments, objections to assessments, appeals, interest, penalties and excess refunds, and the provisions of Part XV (except section 221) and subsections 248(7) and (11) of that Act apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, in relation to any amount paid or payable as or on account of the contributions for a year in respect of self-employed earnings as though that amount were an amount paid or payable as or on account of tax under that Act.
@ref Act s 36 (src:833-834)
GIVEN `the amount is paid or payable as or on account of the contributions for a year in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the Regulations that apply under section 36 (piece cr1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36 — the listed provisions of the Income Tax Act apply to the amount as though it were tax` `the amount is paid or payable as or on account of the contributions for a year in respect of self-employed earnings` `a regulation otherwise provides` MEANS
        `the amount is paid or payable as or on account of the contributions for a year in respect of self-employed earnings`
    AND (NOT `a regulation otherwise provides`)

-- Section 37: a payment made on account of both income tax (section 228 of the Income Tax Act) and contributions in respect of
-- self-employed earnings, "despite any direction made by the person making the payment": the part that section 228 would apply to
-- tax goes to the contributions; the rest goes to tax. The text does not cap the part applied to contributions at what is owing
-- (fork F22). Where the payment is not on account of both, the section does not apply (NOTHING).
-- src:835 | Priority in which payment to be applied
-- src:836 | 37 If any payment is made by a person to the Minister on account of taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and of contributions under this Act in respect of self-employed earnings, despite any direction made by the person making the payment with respect to its application, the part of the payment that would be applied under that section in payment of tax under the Income Tax Act shall be applied in payment of the contributions under this Act and is deemed to be a payment on account of those contributions, and to the extent of the amount so applied shall not discharge liability for tax under the Income Tax Act, and any amount then remaining shall be applied in payment of tax under the Income Tax Act and shall discharge the liability of the person making the payment for that tax to the extent of that amount.
@ref Act s 37 (src:835-836)
GIVEN `the payment is made on account of both taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and contributions in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the payment that would be applied under section 228 of the Income Tax Act in payment of tax` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not deposited
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 37 — the part of the payment applied to the contributions` `the payment is made on account of both taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and contributions in respect of self-employed earnings` `the amount of the payment` `the part of the payment that would be applied under section 228 of the Income Tax Act in payment of tax` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made on account of both taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and contributions in respect of self-employed earnings`
    THEN JUST (min `the amount of the payment` `the part of the payment that would be applied under section 228 of the Income Tax Act in payment of tax`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 37 (src:835-836)
GIVEN `the payment is made on account of both taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and contributions in respect of self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the payment that would be applied under section 228 of the Income Tax Act in payment of tax` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 37 — the part of the payment applied to tax under the Income Tax Act` `the payment is made on account of both taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and contributions in respect of self-employed earnings` `the amount of the payment` `the part of the payment that would be applied under section 228 of the Income Tax Act in payment of tax` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made on account of both taxes specified in section 228 of the Income Tax Act and contributions in respect of self-employed earnings`
    THEN JUST (`the amount of the payment` MINUS (min `the amount of the payment` `the part of the payment that would be applied under section 228 of the Income Tax Act in payment of tax`))
    ELSE NOTHING
